# Line endings, decided once.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout converts to CRLF, the bundler writes LF, and
# `git diff --exit-code addon/dist/Claude.gs` reports the whole file as changed
# — so CI fails on Windows for a reason that has nothing to do with the code.
# It is also why committing here warns about LF being replaced on every file,
# every time.
#
# LF in the repository, LF in the working tree, everywhere. Nothing in this
# project needs CRLF: the .cmd written for the Startup folder is generated at
# runtime rather than checked in.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Recorded CLI output. Byte-exact on purpose — these are what the parser is
# tested against, and a line-ending rewrite is a change to the fixture.
*.jsonl -text

# Certificates and keys are never committed (see .gitignore), but if one ever
# arrives it must not be mangled.
*.pem -text
